course: dictionary
lesson: 10563
title: Unclear: when the meaning is not sure
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unclear means not easy to understand, see or hear, or not known for sure. The un- at the front means "not", and clear means easy to see or understand, so unclear is the opposite of clear. «It is still unclear what happened» means nobody knows yet.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Unclear promises cause rows» tells you that a promise which is not clearly said can lead to arguments. In a test, an unclear question is one where you cannot tell what to answer. When a maths problem is unclear, ask yourself: what is given, and what is asked?
explain: Unclear can also describe a person: «I'm unclear about the homework» means you are not sure what to do. Test your meaning by swapping in "not sure" or "confusing" and checking that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Un- at the start of a word means "not", so unclear means "not clear".
fact: «Unclear» can mean confusing, not known for sure, or not sure yourself.
fact: «It is still unclear what happened» means nobody knows yet.
fact: «The story rests on a few unclear reports» means the evidence is weak, so scientists doubt it.
fact: A good check: read past the headline, check more than one source, and notice who is speaking.
exercise: «First reports, especially breaking news, are often unclear or wrong.» What does unclear mean here? | Very exciting and fast | *Not yet known for sure | Written in big letters | Read aloud by a famous person
exercise: «Unclear promises cause rows.» What does unclear suggest about the promise? | Very short and fast | *Not clearly said, so people argue | Written in gold | Kept by everyone
exercise: Your teacher's instructions are unclear. What should you do? | Start writing straight away without reading | Guess and hope for the best | *Ask again until you understand | Copy your friend's answer
test: Ana says, "The handwriting on my note is unclear." What does she mean? | It is written in another language | *It is hard to read | It is very neat | It is too long
test: «Scientists doubt most of the candiru reports, which are unclear.» Why? | Because the reports are very long | Because scientists love fish | Because the fish is bigger than a dog | *Because the reports are not clear or certain
exam: «How much they think in words is unclear.» What does unclear mean in this sentence? | Easy to see through | Loud and noisy | *Not known for sure | Very happy
